    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/11/nike-vomero-premium-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Maximal 55/45 mm stack with full-length ZoomX and heel/forefoot Air Zoom units delivers high impact protection; heel/forefoot loading feels suspension-like, but initial contact is reported as mildly firm rather than ultra-soft.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is strongly rockered with noticeable bounce and rebound, giving good energy return at easy/steady paces, but the heavy build (11.6 oz men’s US 9) limits snappiness at faster efforts.",
        "Stability: Wide platform and sole flare, a stiff rocker platform, and a rigid heel counter provide relatively stable lateral support and secure lockdown despite the tall stack, though runners with balance/proprioception issues may still find it too high.",
        "Durability: Durability expectation is rated good; the outsole is relatively full-contact with good traction, and the thicker premium upper materials suggest solid long-term wear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/09/nike-vomero-premium-review-bold-radical.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Extremely soft, maximal cushioning (55 mm heel / 45 mm forefoot) with ZoomX plus dual Air Zoom gives a cloud-like heel and forefoot feel with excellent impact protection for easy and recovery runs.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is very bouncy with strong perceived energy return that helps it feel lighter than its weight, but it is not especially snappy for marathon pace or faster efforts.",
        "Stability: Despite the towering stack, a wide base, rigid extended heel counter, padded rear structure, and midfoot support features make it surprisingly stable laterally, though some testers noted heel-lock/Achilles irritation.",
        "Durability: The excerpt does not provide clear long-term durability evidence; specific outsole wear and material longevity findings are largely not reported."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/nike-vomero-premium-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Extremely plush max-cushion ride with a 55 mm heel / 45 mm forefoot stack, full ZoomX foam, and large heel/forefoot Air Zoom units, giving very soft impact protection at both ends.",
        "Responsiveness: ZoomX plus dual Air Zoom units creates a notably bouncy, springy, energetic ride, adding clear rebound even on easy and long runs.",
        "Stability: Better than expected for the extreme stack height; testers reported secure heel lockdown and said it felt more stable/runnable than anticipated rather than overly wobbly.",
        "Durability: Full rubber outsole coverage and strong rain traction indicate good outsole wear resistance, with no major early durability concerns called out for the reviewed pair."
      ]
    }
